win10xbox: gdi32 exports every D3DKMT* thunk the native dxgi/d3d11/dxcore resolve by name, and GdiDllInitializeWrapper

The native dxgi/d3d11 (machine-emu-d3d, Wine's gdi32 + win32u over core/user) fetch the D3DKMT* entry points of the real
gdi32.dll with GetProcAddress at run time; Wine's gdi32 exports only the subset it uses itself, so the first missing one
(D3DKMTGetSharedResourceAdapterLuid) made CreateDXGIFactory1 fail with STATUS_PROCEDURE_NOT_FOUND. On Windows each export
is a thin wrapper of the win32u syscall NtGdiDdDDI<same suffix> (one pointer argument; NtDxgk<suffix> for the newer ones),
so every such syscall of win32u.spec without a D3DKMT counterpart gets a spec forward `D3DKMTxxx(ptr) win32u.Nt...`. win32u's
stubs are syscall thunks the dispatcher passes through to the host's win32u by name (UseHostD3dkmt).

dxcore.dll calls ext-ms-win-gdi-internal-uap-init-l1-1-0!GdiDllInitializeWrapper at load; Wine's apiset maps that
contract to gdi32.dll, which has no such export (EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB). It is the same no-op as GdiDllInitialize.

